\chapter*{How to read this book}
MuDSL provides composable language-building tools in one C++20 header and
one D module. Chapters 1--37 develop those tools, following the companion
manual. Chapters 38--45 connect them into an implementation workflow.
The final 25 chapters, 46--70, specify and teach MuLL: a terse, embeddable
language whose parser and interpreter live in those same two source files.

The examples use the current public names: \api{MuDSL.hpp}, \api{MuDSL.d},
the C++ namespace \api{dsl} (also \api{mudsl}), and D's \api{MuDSL} module.
MuLL's host interfaces are \api{mull::Runtime} and \api{MuLL.Runtime}.
Complete MuLL listings are executed against both implementations by the
conformance suite. Code fragments in the toolkit chapters illustrate
individual APIs; their companion programs live in \api{examples/}.
